    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/318813": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank (Heart and Vascular Service Line) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank (Heart and Vascular Service Line) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Medicine - Cardiology - 411405 Posting Open Date 04/14/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank (Heart and Vascular Service Line) Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005880 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience/Qualifications Proposed Start Date 11/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Division of Cardiology at the UNC School of Medicine is recruiting for a cardiologist who will serve as inpatient lead for the Heart and Vascular service line at the Medical Center in Chapel Hill, NC. The successful candidate will be Board Certified in Internal Medicine and Board Certified or Board Eligible in Cardiology and will have proficiency in general cardiology, electrophysiology, heart failure or interventional cardiology. The successful applicant will spend 20% of their time as inpatient service lead and have responsibility for coordinating inpatient units between Cardiology, Cardiac Surgery and Vascular Surgery. These responsibilities will cover all heart and vascular inpatient services including floor units, intermediate care units and ICUs. The goal of this position is to coordinate activities across all units including ensuring efficient acceptance of hospital-to-hospital transfers, most effective use of inpatient beds, and effective collaboration across the units. This position will also be responsible for designing and leading new inpatient strategic and operational programs patient throughput and length-of-stay initiatives. Clinical responsibilities will depend upon cardiology subspeciality but will likely include a mixture of inpatient and outpatient cardiology +/- imaging and procedures. Position rank and track (fixed term vs. tenure track vs. variable track) will be dependent upon applicant qualifications and experience. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or DO required. Board Certified in Internal Medicine and Board Certified or Board Eligible in Cardiology with proficiency in general cardiology, electrophysiology, heart failure or interventional cardiology. Well-developed interpersonal and communication skills are essential. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Prior leadership experience and experience with program development are preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements N/A Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/315920 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Briana Marini, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email briana_marini@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324786": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | General Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina General Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Surgery - Gastrointest Surgery - 414015 Posting Open Date 09/01/2026 Application Deadline 09/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title General Surgeon Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006069 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 08/30/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Surgery at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking applications for a full-time academic General Surgeon to join the recently established Section of General Surgery within the Division of GI Surgery. This position will include practice at both UNC Health Care at Hillsborough, as well as the Chapel Hill campuses. They will provide comprehensive general surgery services at UNC Health Care at Hillsborough, supporting the Department’s mission to expand access to high-quality surgical care throughout central North Carolina, while building an elective practice with a focus in abdominal wall reconstruction, foregut, and/or minimally invasive general surgery. UNC Health Care Hillsborough is a 68-bed community hospital that combines the culture of a community hospital with the advanced technology and expertise of UNC Medical Center. The campus includes an outpatient medical office building with clinic and procedure space, growing emergency department volumes, robotic surgery capabilities, and expanded operating room capacity. The Department of Surgery is committed to growing both elective and emergency surgical services at Hillsborough while extending specialty surgical care closer to the communities we serve. Clinical responsibilities will include elective and urgent general surgery, emergency general surgery call coverage, outpatient consultation and follow-up, and collaboration with multidisciplinary teams across the UNC Health system. The successful candidate will work closely with colleagues across the Department of Surgery to ensure seamless coordination of care across campuses. This position is being recruited as an Open Rank, Fixed Term appointment between 0.5 FTE and 1.0 FTE faculty appointment, with academic rank commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. The faculty member will be expected to perform clinical duties while fulfilling the academic responsibilities of an educational institution. Faculty members within the Division of GI Surgery are expected to contribute to the Department’s three core missions of clinical care, education, and research. Individuals who exhibit exceptional skills and achievements may be considered for a leadership position within the Department of Surgery. Leadership roles are not guaranteed and are dependent upon the current needs of our surgical service lines. Faculty members are expected to participate in the education of medical students, residents, and other learners through clinical teaching and mentorship in both the academic medical center and community hospital settings. Candidates with interests in clinical research, outcomes research, quality improvement, health services research, surgical education, global surgery, or other scholarly endeavors are encouraged to apply. Faculty members must demonstrate a commitment to providing exceptional patient-centered surgical care while advancing access to high-quality surgical services in a community practice environment. Candidates should possess expertise in a broad range of general surgical procedures, including with minimally invasive and robotic surgery. The selected candidate must be collaborative, team-oriented, and able to work effectively with colleagues across multiple surgical specialties, hospital campuses, and interdisciplinary care teams. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree. Board Certified or Board Eligible in General Surgery. Eligible for medical licensure in the State of North Carolina. Eligible for hospital privileges at UNC Health facilities. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Interest in expanding access to surgical care within community populations. Experience with elective and emergency general surgery. Interest or experience in minimally invasive and robotic surgical techniques. Commitment to excellence in clinical care, medical education, and academic scholarship. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively in multidisciplinary teams. Demonstrated commitment to patient-centered care, quality improvement, and continuous professional development. Interest in clinical research, outcomes research, surgical education, or quality improvement initiatives is desirable. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act.  This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324572 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Muneera Kapadia, Division Chief of GI Department Contact Telephone or Email muneera@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
