    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324548": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Social Work Practitioner Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Social Work Practitioner Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Psychiatry-CECMH-TailoredCM-412221 Career Area Health Professional (Physician/Nurse/Other) Is this an internal only recruitment? No Posting Open Date 08/26/2026 Application Deadline 09/09/2026 Position Type Permanent Staff (SHRA) Position Title Social Work Practitioner - Journey Salary Grade Equivalent NC11 / GN10 Working Title Social Work Practitioner Position Number 20068390 Vacancy ID P021325 Full-time/Part-time Permanent/Time-Limited Full-Time Permanent If time-limited, estimated duration of appointment Hours per week 40 Work Schedule Monday – Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm Work Location CHAPEL HILL, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range $45,000 - $53,000 Pay Band Information To learn more about the pay band for this branch and role, please see the Career Banding rates spreadsheet . Notice to Applicants This position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. Position Summary Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary This position will serve as a Care Manager for the Center for Excellence in Community Mental Health ( CECMH ). The care management team at the CECMH offers robust and effective service models to address the comprehensive health needs of eligible beneficiaries through collaboration with insurance providers, UNC providers, and community partners. This position will provide care management services to an assigned panel of adults with serious mental illness and other behavioral health needs. The Care Manager will engage with assigned beneficiaries through frequent contact based on client need and acuity and will be responsible for ensuring referrals to psychiatry/medication management, therapy, participation in care team huddles, and development of individualized care plans. The Care Manager will also be responsible for monitoring care and ensuring timely hospital follow-up appointments and transitions of care. Due to the nature of this role, the Care Manager is expected to provide services in community-based settings and conduct field visits as needed. Reliable transportation is required to successfully perform the essential functions of the position. This position will complete required trainings and learning activities through UNC CECMH on topics including HIPAA /confidentiality, proficient use of the electronic medical record, corporate compliance and ethics, cultural competence, client rights, workplace safety, and other areas relevant to the population served. In collaboration with the Care Management Program Supervisor, this position will maintain current knowledge of the care management model, policies, procedures, and expectations as disseminated through relevant partners. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Bachelor’s degree in a Human Services discipline with coursework related to the area of assignment. Some positions may require certification to practice as a certified or licensed Clinical Social Worker as required by the North Carolina Social Work Certification Board. Management Preferences Work experience with the population served (adults with serious, persistent mental illness). Experience in case management or care coordination. Knowledge of service systems and community resources. Required Licenses/Certifications Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Position/Schedule Requirements Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324530 Contact Information Office of Human Resources Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (919) 843-2300 or send an email to employment@unc.edu Please note: The Office of Human Resources will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the response below that best describes your experience/education for the Social Work Practitioner position. Bachelor's, Master's or Doctoral degree in a Human Services discipline with coursework related to the area of assignment. None of the above * How many years of experience do you have working with people with serious mental illness? (Open Ended Question) * Are you a licensed clinical social worker? Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319783": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Congenital Heart Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Congenital Heart Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Surgery - Cardiothoracic - 414010 Posting Open Date 04/24/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Congenital Heart Surgeon Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005893 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 09/28/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Surgery at The University of North Carolina is seeking applications for a full-time academic congenital heart surgeon to join our Division of Cardiothoracic Surgery. The Division of Cardiothoracic Surgery is among 9 clinical Divisions in the Department of Surgery. The Division currently includes 8 faculty members that provide exceptional care to patients from across the state of North Carolina. Academic appointment will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience. Exceptional candidates demonstrating outstanding skill and achievement may be considered for additional leadership opportunities within the Department of Surgery; these roles are contingent upon departmental needs at the time of appointment. The ideal candidate will be mid to late career with a proven track record and requisite experience in all aspects of congenital cardiac surgery. The chosen candidate will be expected to work closely and partner with the current congenital heart surgeon and others on the congenital heart team. The breadth of responsibilities will include neonatal cardiac surgery, pediatric heart failure, transplantation, ECMO , and adult congenital surgery. Preference will be given to individuals who bring unique skills, interests or qualifications to the current faculty in a complementary fashion. Individuals with a strong interest in research are encouraged to apply. Faculty members within the Division of Cardiothoracic Surgery must possess a desire to commit to all three missions of the Department of Surgery and School of Medicine, including the clinical, education, and research missions. Regarding the education mission, faculty members are expected to regularly participate in the education of medical students, residents, and fellows. Regarding research, a commitment to any one of a broad array of research interests is desirable, including but not limited to clinical trials, outcomes/health services, basic science, translational, ethics, education, or global surgery research. Regarding the clinical mission, faculty members must be committed to delivering high quality clinical care that is of value to the patients of UNC . Selected candidate must be team-oriented and have the ability to interact well with colleagues inside and out of the Division. This position is being recruited as an open-rank, open-track appointment at an FTE between 0.5 FTE and 1.0 FTE . The appointment may also be offered as a fixed term track or tenure/tenure track appointment. The faculty member will be expected to perform both clinical and research duties, along with the academic responsibilities of an educational institution. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or DO. Chosen candidate should either have a current North Carolina Medical License or be eligible for application. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Completion of an ACGME approved Cardiothoracic Surgery Residency and Congenital Cardiac Surgery fellowship is preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act.  This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/316594 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Elizabeth Hubbard, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email elizabeth_hubbard@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324845": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Director of PATH Services",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Director of PATH Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Director of PATH Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Student Aff Student Wellness-640701 Career Area Student Services Posting Open Date 09/02/2026 Application Deadline 09/23/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Staff (EHRA NF) Working Title Director of PATH Services Appointment Type EHRA Non-Faculty Position Number 01000814 Vacancy ID NF0009996 Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Permanent FTE 1 Hours per week 40 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Commensurate with education and experience Proposed Start Date 10/12/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit UNC -Chapel Hill’s Prevention, Advocacy, Therapy, & Harm Reduction ( PATH ) program serves as a vital co-curricular and Student Success partner in supporting students and the broader campus community regarding substance use education and prevention, risk awareness and mitigation, confidential therapeutic services and case management, and a robust collegiate recovery program.  Through partnerships with other campus departments, community agencies, student organizations, and peer mentors, we use evidence-based public health and social work strategies to foster an environment that creates, emphasizes, and supports healthy choices and positive decision-making.  We utilize a whole-person, student-centered, non-judgmental, and supportive approach, and are seeking experienced professionals to join our interdisciplinary team. Position Summary PATH Prevention, Advocacy, Therapeutic Support & Harm Reduction   is UNC Chapel Hill’s comprehensive substance use services program within the Division of Student Affairs/Student Success, delivering an integrated continuum of care spanning population-level prevention, evidence-based clinical interventions, referrals and case management, risk mitigation and harm reduction strategies, and collegiate recovery support to UNC -Chapel Hill’s more than 32,000 students. Reporting to the Executive Director of Health and Wellbeing, the Director of PATH Services provides strategic leadership, administrative oversight, and operational direction for the University’s comprehensive substance use prevention, intervention, and recovery program. This position establishes PATH’s strategic plan, goals, measurable objectives, and evaluation framework; directly supervises four professional staff (an Administrative Assistant, a Licensed Clinical Addictions Specialist, a Prevention & Harm Reduction Coordinator, and a Recovery Programs Coordinator); manages the program budget across multiple fund sources (state allocation, student fees, grants, and philanthropy); and serves as the University’s principal subject matter expert, internal consultant, and external voice on substance use health, policy, and student welfare. The Director holds clinical credibility sufficient to provide meaningful oversight of PATH’s clinical services   including SBIRT , brief motivational intervention, clinical substance use counseling, warm-handoff referral, and re-entry case management   while operating as a public health systems leader who works upstream to shift campus culture and downstream to support individual students. The Director builds and sustains relationships across a wide range of constituencies, including students in recovery, residence life and Greek life, staff, parents, campus health and counseling partners, senior University leadership, and community coalition partners, adjusting register and approach for each. Standard work schedule Monday through Friday, 9:00am-5:00pm, with regular on-campus presence expected for student accessibility, staff supervision, and partner engagement. Occasional evening and weekend availability required, particularly during high-risk campus periods (orientation, move-in, homecoming, major athletic events, spring break, finals). Some regional and national travel expected for professional conferences and coalition participation. This is the inaugural leadership role for PATH , which is newly established and aspires to become a national model among public flagship universities. The Director is responsible for naming, branding, and institutionally anchoring the program. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Relevant post-Baccalaureate degree required (or foreign degree equivalent); for candidates demonstrating comparable independent educational or instructional activities associated with the delivery and/or management of student support functions, will accept a relevant Bachelor’s degree (or foreign degree equivalent) and at least 1 year of relevant experience in substitution. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Progressively responsible post-master’s experience in substance use prevention, intervention, and recovery supports. Demonstrated supervisory or management experience, including hiring, training, evaluating, and supporting professional staff. Demonstrated experience working in or closely with higher education settings at the four-year or graduate level, with understanding of college student development and campus culture. Demonstrated experience with collegiate recovery programming and working knowledge of ARHE standards. Demonstrated experience with program development, implementation, and assessment, including designing evaluation strategies and using data to improve programming. Demonstrated experience managing departmental or program budgets from multiple fund sources, including grants, student fees, and/or state allocations. Demonstrated knowledge of clinical/sub-clinical concepts, compliance, and processes related to substance use services, with the ability to support clinical staff. Working knowledge of evidence-based prevention frameworks ( SAMHSA Strategic Prevention Framework, NIAAA CollegeAIM, socio-ecological model). Clinical fluency across the substance use disorder spectrum, including current knowledge of fentanyl contamination risk and opioid overdose response. Understanding of federal and North Carolina legal frameworks governing substance use services in higher education, including FERPA , HIPAA , DFSCA , the NC Good Samaritan/Overdose Prevention Act, and ADA /Section 504 as applied to students in recovery. Must complete FERPA and HIPAA compliance training within 30 days of hire and maintain annual compliance. Responsible for handling sensitive and confidential student health information, requiring discretion and compliance with applicable privacy laws, including 42 CFR . Knowledge of CAS , NASPA , ACHA , and ARHE standards as applied frameworks for program quality. Exceptional communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills with demonstrated cultural competence. Demonstrated commitment to equity, cultural humility, and trauma-informed service delivery. Demonstrated ability to build and sustain relationships with diverse stakeholders and to communicate data findings accessibly to non-technical audiences. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Doctoral degree (DrPH, PhD, EdD, or DSW ) in public health, health education, counseling, social work, higher education, or a related behavioral health field. Experience at a Research 1 (R1) or doctoral flagship public university or comparable large, complex institution. Master Certified Health Education Specialist ( MCHES ) or Certified in Public Health ( CPH ) designation, in addition to clinical licensure. Demonstrated experience managing federal or state grants ( SAMHSA , HRSA , or state opioid settlement-funded programs), including grant writing, compliance monitoring, and reporting. Experience designing, implementing, and coordinating campus or community coalitions or collective impact initiatives, or working as a primary partner within one. Published or presented program evaluation findings, research, or policy work at peer-reviewed venues or national professional conferences ( NASPA , ACHA , ARHE , CADCA , or equivalent). Familiarity with NC statewide behavioral health infrastructure, the NC Division of Mental Health/Developmental Disabilities and Substance Use Services, and the Orange County/Chapel Hill treatment provider landscape. Experience in fundraising, donor stewardship, or development, including writing donor proposals and engaging individual donors and foundations. Demonstrated leadership in the field at state or national levels: committee service, association leadership, or peer mentorship of emerging professionals. If professional licensure applies to your training, your standing must be current, or expected within 6 months of hire: Licensed Clinical Addictions Specialist ( LCAS ) in North Carolina, or LCAS -Associate with an approved supervision plan and documented pathway to full licensure. Equivalent out-of-state clinical licensure ( LCSW , LPC , LMFT , LADC , or equivalent) with demonstrated addictions specialization accepted, with NC licensure or endorsement expected within 12 months of hire. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Primarily sedentary office work involving continuous sitting, talking, hearing, and computer use, with frequent standing, movement across campus, and facilitation of in-person programming. Occasional physical activity associated with community events and outreach tabling. Ability to move up to 25 lbs. with or without accommodation. Role regularly involves exposure to emotionally challenging content (student disclosures of trauma, addiction, crisis, grief, and loss); candidates are expected to maintain a sustainable professional practice including peer consultation and clinical supervision where applicable. Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act.  This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324806 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Jonathan Sauls, Senior Associate Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs Department Contact Telephone or Email jsauls@email.unc.edu Office of Human Resources Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (919) 843-2300 or send an email to employment@unc.edu Please note: The Office of Human Resources will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae / Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the response below that describes your level of education that best or mostly closely satisfies the education requirements for this position. Bachelor’s degree in required discipline(s) listed or related field Bachelor's degree in any field/discipline Master's degree or Doctorate degree in required discipline(s) listed or related field Master's degree or Doctorate degree in any field/discipline None of the above Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/323282": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Academic Genitourinary Pathologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Academic Genitourinary Pathologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload a summary of career goals as the required \"Other Document.\" Please provide the names and contact information for four (4) individuals for the \"List of References.\" Posting Information Posting Information Department Pathology Lab Med - Clinical - 413802 Posting Open Date 05/13/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Academic Genitourinary Pathologist Appointment Type Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0005925 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, is seeking an Academic Genitourinary Pathologist for a tenure-track/tenured, fixed-term, or variable track position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. We are a subspecialized surgical pathology division seeking, and preference will be given to, candidates with fellowship training and/or expertise in Genitourinary Pathology. This position requires expertise in all aspects of Genitourinary Pathology; additionally, experience with adrenal resections and biopsies is preferred. Those who are willing to provide additional coverage in other services areas such as Gastrointestinal, Bone and Soft Tissue Pathology, and/or Cytopathology are also encouraged to apply. Participation in multidisciplinary tumor boards and effective communication with an active clinical care team that provides statewide integrated care is required. The successful candidate will be eligible for membership in the UNC Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Center, with opportunities to collaborate with a robust array of basic, translational, and clinical researchers. In addition to teaching clinical residents and fellows, opportunities are available for teaching in the School of Medicine, Graduate School, and Undergraduate School. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Applicants must have an MD, DO or other MD-equivalent degree, be board-certified or board eligible in Anatomic Pathology, and be eligible to obtain a medical license in North Carolina. This position requires expertise in all aspects of Genitourinary Pathology. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience We are a subspecialized surgical pathology division seeking, and preference will be given to, candidates with fellowship training and/or expertise in Genitourinary Pathology. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Please upload a summary of career goals as the required “Other Document.” Please provide the names and contact information for four (4) individuals for the “List of References.” Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/318452 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Susan Maygarden, Chair of the Search Committee Department Contact Telephone or Email susan.maygarden@unchealth.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325003": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Senior Financial Analytics &amp; Reporting Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Senior Financial Analytics & Reporting Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Executive Reporting and Analytics Sample: Please provide a 1-2 page executive briefing, report narrative, analytical summary, presentation excerpt, or similar work product that demonstrates your ability to communicate complex financial or operational information to leadership audiences. Remove or redact any confidential information. Upload in application documents under \"Media Presentation\" Posting Information Posting Information Department Fin Data Analytics-Reporting-216310 Career Area Accounting/Finance/Auditing Posting Open Date 09/02/2026 Application Deadline 09/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Staff (EHRA NF) Working Title Senior Financial Analytics & Reporting Analyst Appointment Type EHRA Non-Faculty Position Number 20078009 Vacancy ID NF0010001 Full Time/Part Time Full-Time Permanent FTE 1 Hours per week 40 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range 90,000-110,000 Proposed Start Date 10/19/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Finance Data Analytics and Reporting team creates roadmaps for technology and analytic tools necessary for the University’s budget and planning needs. This includes providing critical assistance in data analytics and financial modeling, developing templates, dashboards and long-range financial models for the division. The team also develops standardized data for effective and consistent finance and budget reporting throughout campus and for the UNC System, as well as lead the development and implementation of reporting and data warehouse capabilities, using existing tools and acquiring new systems to achieve the University’s evolving financial objectives. Position Summary INTERNAL ONLY : Internal posting for permanent and SHRA time-limited employees of UNC -Chapel Hill only. This position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement that includes a partially remote work location, consistent with System Office policy. UNC -Chapel Hill employees are generally required to reside within a reasonable commuting distance of their assigned duty station. The Senior Financial Analytics & Reporting Analyst serves as the senior individual contributor within the Financial Data Analytics & Reporting team, supporting the development, maintenance, and enhancement of financial reporting, analytics, dashboards, and data solutions that support the University’s budget, planning, and operational decision-making processes. The position partners with Finance, Human Resources, ITS , and campus stakeholders to deliver accurate, consistent, and actionable financial information. The role applies advanced analytical expertise to financial reporting, budgeting, forecasting, data validation, and business intelligence initiatives. This role requires extensive knowledge of UNC -Chapel Hill financial systems, business processes, and institutional data structures, as well as a comprehensive understanding of how financial and HR data interact to support budgeting, compensation analysis, position management, and long-range financial forecasting. The position routinely integrates information from financial, payroll, and human resources systems to provide a complete view of the University’s financial and operational performance. Deep understanding of the University’s chartfield structure, funding sources, position funding methodology, budget development processes, and institutional financial controls is essential to ensure the accuracy and consistency of reporting used by campus leadership and external stakeholders. The position must understand how employee and position data flow through payroll, budgeting, and financial systems and how changes in workforce activity affect institutional budgets, forecasts, and financial performance. Because the role supports critical recurring financial reporting, annual budget development, workforce planning, financial forecasting, and executive decision-making, a thorough working knowledge of UNC -Chapel Hill-specific financial and HR processes is necessary to ensure continuity of operations and maintain the integrity of institutional reporting. This position provides expert guidance on financial business processes, reporting requirements, data governance, and interpretation of complex financial and workforce data, enabling campus leaders to make informed decisions based on reliable and consistent information. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Mid- to late-career with Master’s and 2- 4 years experience; Bachelor’s and 3-5 years experience. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience * Demonstrated expertise in financial management, budgeting, and reporting processes, preferably within UNC or a comparable higher education environment. * Strong understanding of financial data structures and their relationship to HR/payroll data, including implications for budgeting, forecasting, and financial analysis. * Proven ability to lead and deliver complex financial reporting and analytics initiatives that support executive and operational decision-making. * Experience interpreting financial data and translating it into clear, actionable insights for leadership audiences. * Knowledge of internal controls, data validation practices, and financial reporting standards to ensure accuracy and consistency. * Ability to operate independently and exercise sound judgment in resolving complex financial data and reporting issues. * Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present financial information clearly to non-technical stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience * Direct experience working with UNC financial and HR systems, including knowledge of financial reporting practices. * Experience supporting school- or division-level budgeting, forecasting, or long-range financial planning processes. * Familiarity with public higher education finance, including UNC System reporting requirements. * Experience partnering with Finance and HR leaders to develop standardized financial reporting and performance metrics. * Experience interpreting and reconciling financial, payroll, and HR data to support budgeting, forecasting, and decision-making. * Experience contributing to financial system implementations, reporting transformations, or process improvement initiatives. * Experience working with enterprise financial systems (e.g., PeopleSoft) in support of financial operations and reporting. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Executive Reporting and Analytics Sample: Please provide a 1-2 page executive briefing, report narrative, analytical summary, presentation excerpt, or similar work product that demonstrates your ability to communicate complex financial or operational information to leadership audiences. Remove or redact any confidential information. Upload in application documents under “Media Presentation” Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324709 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Brian Lawrence HR Specialist Department Contact Telephone or Email brian_lawrence@unc.edu Office of Human Resources Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (919) 843-2300 or send an email to employment@unc.edu Please note: The Office of Human Resources will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Media Presentation Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the response below that describes your level of education that best or mostly closely satisfies the education requirements for this position. Bachelor’s degree in required discipline(s) listed or related field Bachelor's degree in any field/discipline Master's degree or Doctorate degree in required discipline(s) listed or related field Master's degree or Doctorate degree in any field/discipline None of the above * Are you a current permanent or SHRA time-limited employee of UNC-Chapel Hill? Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/313787": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate - PACE",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate - PACE Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Research Associate - PACE Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department SOP-Practice Advancement - 452500 Posting Open Date 02/18/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Research Associate - PACE Vacancy ID PDS004781 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on experience and qualification. Proposed Start Date 07/01/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC Eshelman School of Pharmacy (www.pharmacy.unc.edu) is one of six health science schools (Pharmacy, Nursing, Dentistry, Social Work, Public Health, Medicine) at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and is one of the oldest health science academic programs at Chapel Hill. The School teaches approximately 600 PharmD students and 145 graduate students. The School has built a reputation for its continued pursuit of excellence, rigorous education and training programs, cutting-edge multidisciplinary research, progressive pharmacy practices, efficient business operations, and its outstanding faculty, staff, and students. The School was named the number one School of Pharmacy in the U.S. by the U.S. News and World Report. The School has experienced unprecedented growth and success and continues to strategically position itself for sustained impact, as articulated in the School’s Strategic Plan (https://pharmacy.unc.edu/about/oe/strategic-plan/). Our Vision is to be the global leader in pharmacy and pharmaceutical sciences. Our Mission is to prepare leaders and innovators to solve the world’s most pressing health care challenges. We are Advancing Medicine for Life through innovation and collaboration in pharmacy practice, education, research, and public service. Position Summary Successful completion of the UNC Eshelman School of Pharmacy Community Practice Fellowship will enable the fellow to become a future faculty member who will be able to lead a successful practice-based research program. The fellowship focuses on the trifold mission of pharmacy faculty – teaching, service, and scholarship. As such, the program will provide the fellow with a solid foundation to begin a productive career in academic pharmacy. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements The candidate must have a Doctor of Pharmacy degree and have completed a PGY1 Community Pharmacy Residency, a PGY1 Pharmacy Practice Residency with an emphasis in ambulatory care, or have equivalent practice experience. The candidate should also be eligible for licensure in the state of North Carolina. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Doctor of Pharmacy degree and be eligible for licensure in the state of North Carolina. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Demonstrate an interest in community pharmacy and academic practice and have an understanding of emerging trends in community pharmacy practice. Demonstrate project management experience; Demonstrate experience leading or engaging in complex collaborative efforts to achieve desired outcomes; Critical thinking and challenge the status quo to arrive at solutions with the greatest potential for impact; Effectively communicate and collaborate with others; Complete work to the highest academic standards; and Ability to multitask and prioritize responsibilities and activities. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/313431 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Alekya Padmanabhuni, HR Business Partner Department Contact Telephone or Email alekya@email.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Writing/research Sample Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Articulate your vision for community pharmacy practice (Open Ended Question) Describe your personal strengths (Open Ended Question) What is your teaching philosophy and how have you incorporated this into your teaching experiences? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324391": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Trainee Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Trainee Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Lineberger Compr Cancer Center - 426801 Posting Open Date 08/24/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Trainee Vacancy ID PDS004951 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Qualiifications Proposed Start Date 10/01/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Liu Lab at UNC Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Center is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Trainee in cancer signaling and cancer biology. The successful candidate will use complementary biochemical, molecular, cellular, and genetic approaches to address fundamental questions in cancer biology and therapeutic response. The fellow will integrate information from diverse experimental systems-including in vitro biochemical and molecular assays, cellular models, and in vivo genetic screens- to develop, test, and validate mechanistic hypotheses with potential therapeutic relevance. This position offers an opportunity to work at the intersection of cancer signaling, molecular biology, and therapeutic discovery, with a strong emphasis on translating mechanistic insights into new strategies for cancer treatment. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Ph.D. in a related field Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Ph.D. in a related field Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Ph.D. in cell biology, biochemistry, biological or biomedical related sciences Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324385 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Joey Landry, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email Joey_Landry@med.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
