ition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Adjunct Clinical Instructor contributes to the educational and academic mission of the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery through participation in departmental educational initiatives, professional development activities, and other scholarly endeavors. The individual may provide substantive experience and expertise to support the development and enhancement of educational programs and continuing education opportunities for clinical professionals within the department. Responsibilities include contributing experience and expertise to departmental educational initiatives, supporting professional development and continuing education activities, collaborating with faculty and departmental leadership on educational projects as appropriate, and participating in other academic and educational activities throughout the year and on an as-needed basis in support of the department’s mission. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Master’s degree with experience in orthopaedic care Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Master’s degree with experience in orthopaedic care Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.