    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/318748": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Maxillofacial Prosthodontist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Maxillofacial Prosthodontist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department ASOD Prosthodontics - 436540 Posting Open Date 11/06/2025 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Maxillofacial Prosthodontist Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005724 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC Adams School of Dentistry Division of Comprehensive Oral Health houses several disciplines including, Periodontology, Dental Hygiene, Comprehensive Dentistry, Operative Dentistry/BioMaterials, Prosthodontics, and Endodontics. The Prosthodontics discipline focuses on the restoration and replacement of teeth and/or craniofacial structures. Strategic Plan – UNC School of Dentistry Position Summary The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Adams School of Dentistry invites applications for a faculty position in Maxillofacial Prosthodontics within the Department of Restorative Sciences. This faculty member will hold a fixed-term or tenure-track appointment commensurate with the candidate’s experience, academic accomplishments, and career goals. Position Summary: The successful candidate will contribute to the school’s mission through excellence in teaching, clinical care, research, and service. Responsibilities include: Providing didactic and clinical instruction and mentoring to predoctoral and postdoctoral students in removable and fixed prosthodontics, implant dentistry, digital dentistry, and maxillofacial prosthodontics. Delivering comprehensive diagnosis, treatment planning, and prosthetic rehabilitation for patients with congenital or acquired craniofacial defects. Participating in interdisciplinary care with colleagues across UNC Health Care and the Health Sciences Schools (Medicine, Nursing, Public Health, and Pharmacy). Engaging in scholarly activities, including clinical or translational research, and contributing to the advancement of the field. Participating in continuing education, faculty development, and professional service at the local, national, or international level. Opportunities Include Intramural practice through the UNC Dental Faculty Practice, with options for hospital privileges and practice in a hospital setting. Interdisciplinary research and clinical collaboration with UNC’s world-class academic health center. Access to state-of-the-art facilities, including digital dentistry technologies and advanced simulation labs. Continuing education and professional service. We welcome applications from candidates who are passionate about advancing the field of maxillofacial prosthodontics through education, clinical care, and research. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Minimum Qualifications: DDS / DMD or equivalent degree Certificate from a CODA -accredited post-graduate prosthodontics program Additional Training and Experience in Maxillofacial prosthodontics. Excellent clinical credentials and experience in dental implants Demonstrated teaching and scholarly activity Strong organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preferred Qualifications: Diplomate of the American Board of Prosthodontics or Board Eligibility Experience in interdisciplinary care and collaborative research Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act.  This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/309070 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Ibrahim Duqum, Department Chair Department Contact Telephone or Email duqumi@dentistry.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity office at (919) 966-3576 or send an email to equalopportunity@unc.edu. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Certification/licenses Degree Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324696": {
      "title": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Temporary Housekeeper (3rd Shift) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Temporary Housekeeper (3rd Shift) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This posting will be filling the following positions: 20077508, 20077509, 20077512 and 20077513 Posting Information Posting Information Department Housekeeping Svcs-Zone 06 - 242006 Career Area Housekeeping and General Services Posting Open Date 08/31/2026 Application Deadline 09/08/2026 Position Type Temporary Staff (SHRA) Position Title Temporary Housekeeper (3rd Shift) Position Number 20077508, 20077509, 20077512, 20077513 Vacancy ID S028016 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 Work Schedule Sunday – Thursday, 11:00 PM – 7:00 AM (Ex. The shift begins at 11:00 PM Thurs. and ends at 7:00 AM Friday) Occasional weekend work required; Occasional overtime required. Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range $15.00 - $15.45 per hour Proposed Start Date Estimated Duration of Appointment 6 months or longer Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks that include numerous retail and restaurant discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates for performing arts events. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Housekeeping Services is comprised of a staff of more than 400 employees who provide cleaning service and floor care to more than 40,000 campus customers in the maintenance and operation of the University’s 18 million plus square feet over 300 teaching, research, medical, administrative, residential, athletic and library buildings. Housekeeping Services is committed to fostering a culture of civility and respect for its diverse workforce as part of its commitment to being a leading building and environment services organization within a leading public institution. Position Summary Provides daily routine and detail cleaning of campus building interior and exterior areas, including but not limited to offices, lounges, restrooms, student housing, classrooms, laboratories, entrances, exits, and stairways. General duties include vacuuming, sweeping, mopping, dusting, and trash removal. Position will primarily be responsible for working in on-campus buildings during the academic year, summer break, and between semesters. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Some knowledge of cleaning procedures, ability to follow instructions and to perform medium to heavy physical work; or an equivalent combination of training and experience. NOTE : Some positions may require special licenses or certification. Management Preferences Demonstrated ability to understand and follow work orders Demonstrated ability to understand and follow work product instructions, labels, and directions Ability to follow verbal instructions Special Physical/Mental Requirements Work is routine and repetitive in nature and may require strenuous physical exertion. Applicants must be able to climb stairs and move objects weighing up to 50 lbs., with or without reasonable accommodations. Employees are required to adhere to safety requirements by wearing the appropriate Personal Protective Equipment ( PPE ). Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions This posting will be filling the following positions: 20077508, 20077509, 20077512 and 20077513 Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324669 Temporary Employment Policies Temporary Employment Policies Posting Contact Information Office of Human Resources Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (919) 843-2300 or send an email to employment@unc.edu Please note: The Office of Human Resources will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This is a 3rd shift position.  Are you available to work 11:00pm - 7:00am? Yes No * Are you available to occasionally work overtime, evenings, weekends, and holidays? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to lift or move objects up to 50 pounds with or without an accommodation? yes no * Are you able to serve as a mandatory employee and report to work in support of mandatory University operations even when the University is closed? Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
